{"parentUuid":"1c9f6f22-9602-46eb-b2cf-b41fd67b2b42","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f859c755-da6c-49d3-9404-148b849e4500","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Qa7fJ9cVRGGZZoxa41s1S","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"pi.dev open source agent harness CLI install \"pi\" agentic coding 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"harness-agent · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/harness-agent/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - earendil-works/pi: AI agent toolkit: unified LLM API, agent loop, TUI, coding agent CLI · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - baryonlabs/pi-agent-harness: pi-agent-harness — a pi coding-agent plugin/package that turns one domain sentence into a multi-agent team: specialist agents (.pi/agents), their skills (.pi/skills), and orchestration prompts (.pi/prompts). A team-architecture factory with 6 patterns and a bundled subagent (single/parallel/chain) delegation tool.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/baryonlabs/pi-agent-harness\"},{\"title\":\"Open-Source BYOK CLI Coding Agent (Pi Agent Harness)\",\"url\":\"https://www.llmreference.com/agents/pi\"},{\"title\":\"Pi Coding Agent\",\"url\":\"https://pi.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"Pi: A Coding Agent Harness You Can Reshape Around Your Workflow – silenceper\",\"url\":\"https://silenceper.com/en/article/2026-05-27-pi-coding-agent-harness/\"},{\"title\":\"Pi.dev: A Minimal Terminal Coding Harness | Dev-Ore\",\"url\":\"https://www.dev-ore.com/blog/pi-dev-terminal-coding-harness/\"},{\"title\":\"Pi Agent Harness: An AI Agent Toolkit for LLMs and Coding - OSRepos\",\"url\":\"https://osrepos.com/repo/earendil-works-pi\"},{\"title\":\"Pi Agent Harness (pi.dev): Minimal Coding Agent by Mario Zechner (2026) | explainx.ai Blog | explainx.ai\",\"url\":\"https://explainx.ai/blog/pi-minimal-agent-harness-mario-zechner-guide-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about pi.dev and the open source agent harness CLI:\n\n## Pi Agent Harness Overview\n\nPi is a minimal agent harness, and it's a minimal terminal coding harness from Mario Zechner, now documented at pi.dev under Earendil Inc.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install Pi using curl with `curl -fsSL https://pi.dev/install.sh | sh`, or via npm with `npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`.\n\n## Core Features\n\nPi's built-in tools are read, bash, edit, write, grep, find, and ls, with heavier behavior layered through extensions, skills, prompt templates, themes, and Pi packages. Pi offers a unified API for interacting with multiple Large Language Models (LLMs) like OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google.\n\n## Design Philosophy\n\nThe project keeps the core small and makes the rest open to user extension. Pi documents project trust, sandbox boundaries, and containerization options because the core harness does not ship permission popups — confirmation flows belong in your extension, aligned with your threat model.\n\nThe project is open source (MIT), with documentation at pi.dev/docs/latest and the coding-agent package developed in the monorepo under earendil-works/pi.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"03970b61-498d-4489-8943-4365defa373e","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:32:55.544Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"pi.dev open source agent harness CLI install \"pi\" agentic coding 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013A9EMgRHCEb953t2pk5PPz","content":[{"title":"harness-agent · PyPI","url":"https://pypi.org/project/harness-agent/"},{"title":"GitHub - earendil-works/pi: AI agent toolkit: unified LLM API, agent loop, TUI, coding agent CLI · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/earendil-works/pi"},{"title":"GitHub - baryonlabs/pi-agent-harness: pi-agent-harness — a pi coding-agent plugin/package that turns one domain sentence into a multi-agent team: specialist agents (.pi/agents), their skills (.pi/skills), and orchestration prompts (.pi/prompts). A team-architecture factory with 6 patterns and a bundled subagent (single/parallel/chain) delegation tool.","url":"https://github.com/baryonlabs/pi-agent-harness"},{"title":"Open-Source BYOK CLI Coding Agent (Pi Agent Harness)","url":"https://www.llmreference.com/agents/pi"},{"title":"Pi Coding Agent","url":"https://pi.dev/"},{"title":"Pi: A Coding Agent Harness You Can Reshape Around Your Workflow – silenceper","url":"https://silenceper.com/en/article/2026-05-27-pi-coding-agent-harness/"},{"title":"Pi.dev: A Minimal Terminal Coding Harness | Dev-Ore","url":"https://www.dev-ore.com/blog/pi-dev-terminal-coding-harness/"},{"title":"Pi Agent Harness: An AI Agent Toolkit for LLMs and Coding - OSRepos","url":"https://osrepos.com/repo/earendil-works-pi"},{"title":"Pi Agent Harness (pi.dev): Minimal Coding Agent by Mario Zechner (2026) | explainx.ai Blog | explainx.ai","url":"https://explainx.ai/blog/pi-minimal-agent-harness-mario-zechner-guide-2026"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about pi.dev and the open source agent harness CLI:\n\n## Pi Agent Harness Overview\n\nPi is a minimal agent harness, and it's a minimal terminal coding harness from Mario Zechner, now documented at pi.dev under Earendil Inc.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install Pi using curl with `curl -fsSL https://pi.dev/install.sh | sh`, or via npm with `npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`.\n\n## Core Features\n\nPi's built-in tools are read, bash, edit, write, grep, find, and ls, with heavier behavior layered through extensions, skills, prompt templates, themes, and Pi packages. Pi offers a unified API for interacting with multiple Large Language Models (LLMs) like OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google.\n\n## Design Philosophy\n\nThe project keeps the core small and makes the rest open to user extension. Pi documents project trust, sandbox boundaries, and containerization options because the core harness does not ship permission popups — confirmation flows belong in your extension, aligned with your threat model.\n\nThe project is open source (MIT), with documentation at pi.dev/docs/latest and the coding-agent package developed in the monorepo under earendil-works/pi."],"durationSeconds":7.049135667000199,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1c9f6f22-9602-46eb-b2cf-b41fd67b2b42","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"842a50ac-e2b8-4cf1-a0fa-cfdb700f53f1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f859c755-da6c-49d3-9404-148b849e4500","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YaKQyuUXsuVx2YbRK34CjS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pi Coding Agent Overview\n\n**What is Pi?**\nPi is described as \"a minimal agent harness.\" It's an open-source CLI tool designed for AI-assisted coding that prioritizes customization over rigid workflows.\n\n**Creator**\nEarendil Inc. and contributors developed Pi, with the project available under an MIT License.\n\n**Installation**\nThe exact npm installation command is:\n```\nnpm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\n```\n\nAlternative installers exist for curl, PowerShell, pnpm, and bun.\n\n**Supported Models**\nPi integrates with 15+ providers including Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Azure, Bedrock, Mistral, Groq, Cerebras, xAI, Hugging Face, and others. You can \"Switch models mid-session with `/model` or `Ctrl+L`.\"\n\n**Key Features**\n- Extensible architecture for custom extensions, skills, and themes\n- Tree-structured session history with branching and sharing capabilities\n- Context engineering through AGENTS.md and SYSTEM.md files\n- Four operational modes: interactive TUI, print/JSON, RPC, and SDK\n- Real-time steering of running agents via Enter and Alt+Enter\n- Minimal default system prompt with progressive capability disclosure\n- Support for custom providers and models via configuration files"}]},"uuid":"091b5bb0-ca5d-4be0-bbbb-534575287102","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:32:56.752Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":56230,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Pi Coding Agent Overview\n\n**What is Pi?**\nPi is described as \"a minimal agent harness.\" It's an open-source CLI tool designed for AI-assisted coding that prioritizes customization over rigid workflows.\n\n**Creator**\nEarendil Inc. and contributors developed Pi, with the project available under an MIT License.\n\n**Installation**\nThe exact npm installation command is:\n```\nnpm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\n```\n\nAlternative installers exist for curl, PowerShell, pnpm, and bun.\n\n**Supported Models**\nPi integrates with 15+ providers including Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Azure, Bedrock, Mistral, Groq, Cerebras, xAI, Hugging Face, and others. You can \"Switch models mid-session with `/model` or `Ctrl+L`.\"\n\n**Key Features**\n- Extensible architecture for custom extensions, skills, and themes\n- Tree-structured session history with branching and sharing capabilities\n- Context engineering through AGENTS.md and SYSTEM.md files\n- Four operational modes: interactive TUI, print/JSON, RPC, and SDK\n- Real-time steering of running agents via Enter and Alt+Enter\n- Minimal default system prompt with progressive capability disclosure\n- Support for custom providers and models via configuration files","durationMs":6747,"url":"https://pi.dev"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"842a50ac-e2b8-4cf1-a0fa-cfdb700f53f1","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"091b5bb0-ca5d-4be0-bbbb-534575287102","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"WebFetch","description":"Fetches a URL, converts the page to markdown, and answers `prompt` against it using a small fast model.\n\n- Fails on authenticated/private URLs — use an authenticated MCP tool or `gh` for those instead. Exception: claude.ai artifact links (claude.ai/artifact/{id} or claude.ai/code/artifact/{uuid}) ARE fetchable via your claude.ai login — use WebFetch, not curl (curl gets the SPA shell or a Cloudflare 403).\n- Fails on localhost and other hostnames without a dot; for a local server, use curl via Bash.\n- HTTP is upgraded to HTTPS. Cross-host redirects are returned to you rather than followed; call again with the redirect URL.\n- Responses are cached for 15 minutes per URL.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"url":{"description":"The URL to fetch content from","type":"string","format":"uri"},"prompt":{"description":"The prompt to run on the fetched content","type":"string"}},"required":["url","prompt"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true},{"name":"WebSearch","description":"Search the web. Returns result blocks with titles and URLs. US-only.\n\n- The current month is September 2026 — use this when searching for recent information.\n- `allowed_domains` / `blocked_domains` filter results.\n- After answering from results, end with a \"Sources:\" list of the URLs you used as markdown links.","input_schema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"query":{"description":"The search query to use","type":"string","minLength":2},"allowed_domains":{"description":"Only include search results from these domains","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"blocked_domains":{"description":"Never include search results from these domains","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c4e1bc0a-9a0b-4518-91b7-67b8bce40189","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:32:56.755Z","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
