{"parentUuid":"eed68a1c-4ac9-4355-89b4-a184deb59070","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceydv6gLovTV8Dt8HsEsv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016J8T4bjA5BUftTZ3bBtNUz","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md","old_string":"**Proof demo (7:19–8:55):** Kashef opens LM Studio with local Qwen 2 7B — a raw model with\nno harness — and asks it to build a landing page *and spin up a local server*.\nIt writes the HTML. It cannot start the server. No limbs.\nGive the same prompt to Claude Code or Codex and it does not blink.","new_string":"**Proof demo (7:19–8:55):** Kashef opens LM Studio with a local Qwen model (captions read\n\"Quen 27B\" — likely a 7B-class Qwen, too small on screen to confirm) — a raw brain with no\nharness — and asks it to build a landing page *and spin up a local server*.\nIt writes the HTML. It cannot start the server. No limbs.\nGive the same prompt to Claude Code or Codex and it does not blink.\n\n**The workflow prediction that follows (3:25–3:41):** open-source local models already do\n\"like 80% of the day-to-day work.\" He expects a world within a year where you run\n**70–80% locally** (given the hardware) and only \"bring in the geniuses for genius-level\ntasks or planning.\" The harness is what makes that split possible — the local brain gets\nthe same limbs as the expensive one."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1747,"cache_read_input_tokens":255502,"output_tokens":1307,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":716},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":350,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[