(7:19–8:55):** Kashef opens LM Studio with local Qwen 2 7B — a raw model with","-no harness — and asks it to build a landing page *and spin up a local server*.","+**Proof demo (7:19–8:55):** Kashef opens LM Studio with a local Qwen model (captions read","+\"Quen 27B\" — likely a 7B-class Qwen, too small on screen to confirm) — a raw brain with no","+harness — and asks it to build a landing page *and spin up a local server*."," It writes the HTML. It cannot start the server. No limbs."," Give the same prompt to Claude Code or Codex and it does not blink."," ","+**The workflow prediction that follows (3:25–3:41):** open-source local models already do","+\"like 80% of the day-to-day work.\" He expects a world within a year where you run","+**70–80% locally** (given the hardware) and only \"bring in the geniuses for genius-level","+tasks or planning.\" The harness is what makes that split possible — the local brain gets","+the same limbs as the expensive one.","+"," **The consequence for benchmarks (20:29–21:45):** after the March 2026 Claude Code harness"," leak, Kashef read the whole thing. Most of it was *crutches* — regex lists of swear words,"," behaviour guards, scaffolding. His takeaway:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"53c228d2-1537-45ec-8934-21f166cde0a3","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
