est today can be\nswapped in with near-zero acclimation. If Gemini \"truly wakes up\" tomorrow, he wants the\nswap to cost 24 hours, not a rebuild.\n\n---\n\n## Gap analysis — video claim vs. your actual setup","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":70,"oldLines":6,"newStart":70,"newLines":31,"lines":[" "," ---"," ","+## Hermes, OpenClaw, and Pi — the same category (13:37–15:28)","+","+All three are **bring-your-own-model harnesses**: you supply the harness, then loop in","+whatever brain you want.","+","+- **Hermes beat OpenClaw on the harness, not the skills.** Kashef is blunt at 14:14 —","+  \"all these skill MD files, etc., they're all great, but the thing that made Hermes","+  better than OpenClaw is its harness.\"","+- **Vanilla Hermes loses to Codex.** Run the same task one-to-one, out of the box, and","+  you get a different result. But you can *massage* Hermes's harness until it performs","+  the same verification loop that makes Codex feel sharp. Monkey see, monkey do.","+- **That is why everyone's Hermes agent is a \"special snowflake\"** (14:00) — people keep","+  hacking the harness to fit how they want to use their models.","+- **Pi is the vanilla open-source version** of the same idea (6:03), where you build your","+  own harness from a minimal base.","+","+The endgame he wants (15:34): one harness for everything, with models as a **leased brain**","+you swap out as needed. His framing at 15:47 — the ecosystem is tribal right now","+(\"I am team Codex, I am team Claude Code, you are all Neanderthals\"). He is deliberately","+anti-tribal: build so that whichever brain is best, fastest, or cheapest today can be","+swapped in with near-zero acclimation. If Gemini \"truly wakes up\" tomorrow, he wants the","+swap to cost 24 hours, not a rebuild.","+","+---","+"," ## Gap analysis — video claim vs. your actual setup"," "," | # | Technique (timestamp) | What the video says | Your status | Your equivalent |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":fa