{"parentUuid":"232b4765-15dd-4fae-aacf-860f0cc68a48","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceye8b8TRtS2UzkhUCBEV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verified: the script in the file prints 58 / 30 / 19, matching the table.\n\n## What I did\n\nI watched the whole 34-minute video. I pulled the transcript, grabbed 6 key frames, and checked pi.dev myself. Then I compared it all to your real machine.\n\n**The file is here:**\n`/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`\n\nIt has the big idea, a chapter map, a gap table (11 techniques vs. what you already have), the decay-tier table, the Pi section, and ranked actions.\n\n## The big idea\n\nThe model is a brain in a jar. The **harness** gives it hands and legs. Stop shopping for brains. Build the harness you own.\n\n## The finding that matters most\n\nI counted your machine. This is not from the video:\n\n- **164** global skills + **606** plugin skills installed\n- **58** skills you have *ever* used, across 414 sessions\n- **30** used more than twice\n- **0** project-level skills — everything is global\n\nThe video calls this exact problem out. Their fix is the **promotion rule**: a skill stays project-level until it earns global. You are doing the opposite.\n\n## About Pi\n\nPi is real, open source, MIT, at pi.dev. It gives you 7 tools and nothing else. You build the rest.\n\nTwo things the video does not say:\n1. **Pi ships no permission prompts.** Your `dcg` guard and backup default-deny do not exist there. Never point it at `~/DEV` or `DexaProject`.\n2. **Your skills would port. Your 61 hooks would not.** Those are Claude-Code-shaped. In Pi they get rewritten.\n\n## Your one decision\n\n| Option | Why |\n|---|---|\n| **A. Skill audit first** ⭐ | Cuts 164 skills to ~30. Helps you today, and makes a Pi move cheaper later. |\n| B. Try Pi in a sandbox now | Fun Saturday. But you would port 770 messy skills instead of 30 good ones. |\n\n**I would go A.** Your leverage is the bloat, not the harness.\n\nWant me to save the skill-bloat finding to memory? I did not write it — you said to ask first.\n\nresult: Video fully extracted to `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md` — 11-technique gap table vs. your setup, Pi facts verified at pi.dev with two caveats the video omits, and a measured finding that you have 770 skills installed but have ever used 58."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":135527,"output_tokens":1049,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":197},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1049,"cache_read_input_tokens":135527,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ceye8Vye8tRokhpXS8ukZ","attributionSkill":"watch:watch","attributionPlugin":"watch","type":"assistant","uuid":"92c0d11b-7273-4739-9306-51bf4f260db5","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:41:24.674Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
