{"parentUuid":"3ed5405e-607d-4a3e-ad5e-54ecb175cc32","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeyfCKhFXYQQaAaFxdPNH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No duplicate exists. Writing the Tier A memory file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":141297,"output_tokens":2226,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":362},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":755,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2226,"cache_read_input_tokens":141297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":755},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeyfCJWZ1yJHFazRXfgcy","attributionSkill":"memory-write","type":"assistant","uuid":"d98a1d49-8a67-4fde-90ca-6468005b157b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:55:12.544Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d98a1d49-8a67-4fde-90ca-6468005b157b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeyfCKhFXYQQaAaFxdPNH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015u8d8JQ6ahx6M7FiutmLjL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md","content":"---\nname: skill-bloat-and-promotion\ndescription: \"Measured skill bloat in this setup, the project-until-promoted rule that fixes it, and the command that re-measures usage from .jsonl session logs\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n---\n\nMeasured 2026-09-12 from a gap analysis of a Nate Herk / **Mark Kashef** video\n(\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 2026-09-11). Full note:\n`~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\nSame shape as the earlier audit in [[brain-audit-loop]] — that one scored the\n**vault**, this one scores the **skill layer**.\n\n## The measurement\n\n| Metric | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | 164 |\n| Plugin skills installed | 606 |\n| Exposed to one session's roster | ~120 |\n| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n| `.jsonl` sessions scanned | 414 |\n| Distinct real skills **ever** invoked | **58** |\n| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n| Used exactly once | 19 |\n\nEverything is global. That is the anti-pattern, not the achievement.\n\n## The rule that fixes it — promotion\n\n**Everything stays project-level until it earns global.** A skill lives in\n`<project>/.claude/skills/` until it proves itself across 2+ projects, then it\ngets promoted to `~/.claude/skills/`. Keeps the global load small and the blast\nradius tight — so when something underperforms you can tell a *model* problem\nfrom a *harness* problem from an *organisation* problem.\n\n## The audit question\n\nNot \"how often did I run this skill?\" but **\"would the model do this fine without\nthe skill now?\"** A skill is a crutch; as the brain gets smarter the crutch starts\nto *limit* it. Seasonal skills (`forecast-capture`) and occasional ones\n(`ingest-book`) are low-count by design — low usage alone is not a delete signal.\n\n## Re-measure (BUILTIN filter is the whole trick)\n\nWithout the `BUILTIN` set you also count `/exit`, `/clear`, `/compact` and friends,\nwhich inflates the total to 74 and buries the real skills.\n\n```bash\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport glob,re,collections\nBUILTIN={'exit','clear','compact','rename','color','login','logout','plugin','doctor',\n'help','model','config','resume','cost','status','init','agents','mcp','hooks','memory',\n'review','vim','terminal-setup','install-github-app','add-dir','bug','release-notes',\n'pr-comments','ide','permissions','statusline','output-style','todos','export',\n'privacy-settings','upgrade','fast','artifacts','tasks','loop','context','usage','rewind',\n'sandbox','feedback','worktrees','skills','reload-skills','reload-plugins','bashes',\n'keybindings','theme'}\nc=collections.Counter()\nfor f in glob.glob('/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl',recursive=True):\n    try:\n        for line in open(f,encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore'):\n            if 'Skill' not in line and 'command-name' not in line: continue\n            for m in re.finditer(r'\"name\"\\s*:\\s*\"Skill\"\\s*,\\s*\"input\"\\s*:\\s*\\{[^}]*?\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"([^\"]+)\"', line):\n                c[m.group(1)]+=1\n            for m in re.finditer(r'<command-name>/([a-zA-Z0-9:_-]+)</command-name>', line):\n                c[m.group(1)]+=1\n    except Exception: pass\nreal={k:v for k,v in c.items() if k.split(':')[-1] not in BUILTIN and k not in BUILTIN}\nprint(\"distinct real skills ever invoked:\",len(real))\nprint(\"used >=3 times:\",len([k for k,v in real.items() if v>=3]))\nprint(\"used exactly once:\",len([k for k,v in real.items() if v==1]))\nfor k,v in sorted(real.items(),key=lambda x:-x[1]): print(f\"{v:5d}  {k}\")\nEOF\n```\n\n## Decision, 2026-09-12\n\n**Do the skill audit BEFORE adopting Pi** (`pi.dev`) as an alternative harness.\nRationale: the leverage is the bloat, not the harness. Auditing first means any\nfuture harness move ports ~30 good skills instead of 770 mixed ones.\n\nTwo Pi facts that are easy to get wrong: Pi ships **no permission prompts**\n(confirmation flows are your extension's job — so never run it against `~/DEV` or\nanything touching `DexaProject`), and **skills port but hooks do not** — the 61\nhooks in `~/.claude/hooks/` are Claude-Code-shaped and would be rewritten as Pi\nextensions. See also [[hook-two-copies-trap]] and [[dcg-guard-blocks]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":141297,"output_tokens":2226,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":362},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":755,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2226,"cache_read_input_tokens":141297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":755},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CeyfCJWZ1yJHFazRXfgcy","attributionSkill":"memory-write","type":"assistant","uuid":"e6ef50d9-90a5-4d24-94ce-78b4147f7482","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:55:33.325Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
