{"parentUuid":"83224709-4c47-4219-b463-108c04ac1e05","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e343e296-cde7-42eb-aa45-e11d4469cccf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KiyUDSo9zXncfgbwRQBujb","type":"tool_result","content":"=== pbir-report-builder ===\ndescription: \"Generates Power BI report pages, visuals, and IBCS-compliant variance charts by writing PBIR JSON into PBIP project folders. Use whenever the user wants to create a Power BI page, add visuals, generate KPI cards, build charts, tables or dashboard layouts, or mentions 'PBIR', 'IBCS', 'variance chart', 'variance table', 'actual vs plan'.\"\n---\n\n# PBIR Report Builder\n=== Telos ===\ndescription: \"Dual-context skill. Personal TELOS: read and update goals, beliefs, wisdom, frames, wrong-beliefs in `~/.claude/LIFEOS/USER/TELOS/` via the Update workflow with timestamped backups. Storage is a SYMLINK to `~/.config/LIFEOS/USER` — measure it with `du -shL` / `find -L`, or it looks empty. Project TELOS: analyze .md/.csv directories to extract dependency chains (PROBLEMS→GOALS→STRATEGIES→PROJECTS), bottlenecks, alignment, progress metrics; generate McKinsey-style WriteReport, n=24 CreateNarrativePoints, or Next.js dashboards via parallel engineers. Also InterviewExtraction. USE WHEN Telos, my goals, my beliefs, add to TELOS, life frames, mental models, what am I wrong about, projects, dependencies, narrative points, McKinsey report, dashboard. NOT FOR conversational constitutional review (use Interview).\"\neffort: medium\n=== visual-explainer ===\ndescription: >\n  Generate a beautiful, self-contained HTML page that visually explains any system, concept, plan,\n  or data. Use this skill when the user says \"explain this visually\", \"visual explainer\",\n  \"make a diagram page\", \"interactive explanation\", \"visualize this\", \"explain this to my team\",\n=== Interceptor ===\ndescription: \"Real Chrome/Brave + macOS Computer Use from inside the browser — zero CDP fingerprint, real sessions, six verb trees (References/CommandReference.md). REQUIRES the `interceptor` binary on PATH: run the Preflight block first and STOP if it fails — where it is absent use claude-in-chrome (interactive/authenticated) or playwright-cli (scripted/headless). Preferred for visual deploy verification on machines where it IS installed. Drive clickwork yourself, never narrate it. USE WHEN verify deploy, confirm UI, screenshot verification, computer use, macos automation, debug web, console logs/errors, runtime/JS/react errors, network traffic/log, HAR/pcapng export, hydration/blank-page debug, authenticated page, bot detection bypass, reproduce bug, drive native app, OAuth consent flow, complete a web login. NOT FOR batch headless automation (Browser), residential-proxy crawling (BrightData), social actor scraping (Apify), or any machine where `interceptor --version` fails (use claude-in-chrome).\"\nversion: 4.3.0\n=== pp-espn ===\ndescription: \"ESPN sports CLI — live scores, standings, team stats, schedules, polls, rankings, and game summaries (box score, leaders, scoring plays, odds, win probability) across NFL / NBA / MLB / NHL / NCAA / MLS / EPL / WNBA. Use for 'what's the score of the Lakers game', 'Patriots schedule this week', 'NFL standings', 'box score', head-to-head comparisons, 'who's on top of the AP poll'. No API key required.\"\r\nauthor: \"Matt Van Horn\"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5fd0ddaa-0c99-4f7d-ac13-ef6b8671d804","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:57:29.437Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== pbir-report-builder ===\ndescription: \"Generates Power BI report pages, visuals, and IBCS-compliant variance charts by writing PBIR JSON into PBIP project folders. Use whenever the user wants to create a Power BI page, add visuals, generate KPI cards, build charts, tables or dashboard layouts, or mentions 'PBIR', 'IBCS', 'variance chart', 'variance table', 'actual vs plan'.\"\n---\n\n# PBIR Report Builder\n=== Telos ===\ndescription: \"Dual-context skill. Personal TELOS: read and update goals, beliefs, wisdom, frames, wrong-beliefs in `~/.claude/LIFEOS/USER/TELOS/` via the Update workflow with timestamped backups. Storage is a SYMLINK to `~/.config/LIFEOS/USER` — measure it with `du -shL` / `find -L`, or it looks empty. Project TELOS: analyze .md/.csv directories to extract dependency chains (PROBLEMS→GOALS→STRATEGIES→PROJECTS), bottlenecks, alignment, progress metrics; generate McKinsey-style WriteReport, n=24 CreateNarrativePoints, or Next.js dashboards via parallel engineers. Also InterviewExtraction. USE WHEN Telos, my goals, my beliefs, add to TELOS, life frames, mental models, what am I wrong about, projects, dependencies, narrative points, McKinsey report, dashboard. NOT FOR conversational constitutional review (use Interview).\"\neffort: medium\n=== visual-explainer ===\ndescription: >\n  Generate a beautiful, self-contained HTML page that visually explains any system, concept, plan,\n  or data. Use this skill when the user says \"explain this visually\", \"visual explainer\",\n  \"make a diagram page\", \"interactive explanation\", \"visualize this\", \"explain this to my team\",\n=== Interceptor ===\ndescription: \"Real Chrome/Brave + macOS Computer Use from inside the browser — zero CDP fingerprint, real sessions, six verb trees (References/CommandReference.md). REQUIRES the `interceptor` binary on PATH: run the Preflight block first and STOP if it fails — where it is absent use claude-in-chrome (interactive/authenticated) or playwright-cli (scripted/headless). Preferred for visual deploy verification on machines where it IS installed. Drive clickwork yourself, never narrate it. USE WHEN verify deploy, confirm UI, screenshot verification, computer use, macos automation, debug web, console logs/errors, runtime/JS/react errors, network traffic/log, HAR/pcapng export, hydration/blank-page debug, authenticated page, bot detection bypass, reproduce bug, drive native app, OAuth consent flow, complete a web login. NOT FOR batch headless automation (Browser), residential-proxy crawling (BrightData), social actor scraping (Apify), or any machine where `interceptor --version` fails (use claude-in-chrome).\"\nversion: 4.3.0\n=== pp-espn ===\ndescription: \"ESPN sports CLI — live scores, standings, team stats, schedules, polls, rankings, and game summaries (box score, leaders, scoring plays, odds, win probability) across NFL / NBA / MLB / NHL / NCAA / MLS / EPL / WNBA. Use for 'what's the score of the Lakers game', 'Patriots schedule this week', 'NFL standings', 'box score', head-to-head comparisons, 'who's on top of the AP poll'. No API key required.\"\r\nauthor: \"Matt Van Horn\"","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"83224709-4c47-4219-b463-108c04ac1e05","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
