{"parentUuid":"60d3f54b-0589-4e07-8dce-f9d328d4d873","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-skill-audit.md","snippet":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: \"Skill audit 2026-09-12 — 160 global skills down to 60\"\n3\tdate: 2026-09-12\n4\ttype: audit\n5\ttrigger: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6LNlCpQPYFc\n6\trelated: 2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md\n7\tscript: ~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh\n8\ttags: [skills, context-engineering, claude-code, audit]\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t# Skill audit — 2026-09-12\n12\t\n13\t> ## STATUS\n14\t> - **Tier 1: EXECUTED 2026-09-12.** 43 skills archived to\n15\t>   `~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/`. Global skills 160 → **117**.\n16\t>   Regression check clean — **none** of the 43 had ever been invoked.\n17\t>   Roster cost 19,158 → **12,495 tokens** per session.\n18\t> - **Tier 2: NOT RUN.** 56 skills, ~6,137 tokens. Awaiting review.\n19\t> - Hook safety checked: `ArtWorkflowGuard` and `containment-zones` reference\n20\t>   archived paths but both degrade safely (try/catch → `[]`, and static strings).\n21\t>   Nothing broke.\n22\t> - **Do not re-run `tier1`.** It is already done.\n23\t\n24\tTriggered by the Mark Kashef / Nate Herk harness video. Companion note:\n25\t`2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md`.\n26\t\n27\t## The bill (as measured *before* Tier 1 ran)\n28\t\n29\t| | |\n30\t|---|---|\n31\t| Global skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | **160** |\n32\t| — of which are symlinks into `~/.agents/skills/` | 45 |\n33\t| Plugin skills exposed per session | ~37 (6 plugins enabled, 18 disabled) |\n34\t| SKILL.md files in plugin cache | 606 — mostly disabled plugins and old versions, **not** the load |\n35\t| Project-level skills anywhere in `~/DEV` | **0** |\n36\t| Distinct skills ever invoked (414 sessions) | **58** |\n37\t| Used 3+ times | 30 |\n38\t| Never used at all | **130** |\n39\t| **Context cost of the skill roster, every session** | **~19,158 tokens** |\n40\t\n41\tThat last row is the real cost. Every skill's name and description is loaded into\n42\tcontext at session start whether you use it or not. 19k tokens is the standing tax.\n43\t\n44\t## The rule applied\n45\t\n46\tThe video's audit question is not *\"how often did I run this?\"* It is:\n47\t\n48\t> **\"Would the model do this fine without the skill now?\"**\n49\t\n50\tA skill is a crutch. As the brain gets smarter, the crutch starts to limit it.\n51\tSo the keep/cut split below is by **category**, not by usage count.\n52\t\n53\t## Verified before cutting\n54\t\n55\t- `interceptor`, `firecrawl`, `playwright`, `bright-data`, `apify` — **all missing\n56\t  from PATH.** Those skills can never fire successfully. Pure dead weight.\n57\t- **45 skills are symlinks** into `~/.agents/skills/`, the folder Codex and Cowork\n58\t  also read. Archiving a symlink de-registers it from Claude Code and **leaves the\n59\t  real skill intact for Codex.** That is the desired behaviour, not a side effect.\n60\t  (Related: `project_vendored-skill-install`, `project_vendored-skill-repair`.)\n61\t- 13 skills were installed in the last 14 days. They get a grace period — too new\n62\t  to judge. Not in any cut tier.\n63\t\n64\t## The tiers\n65\t\n66\t### Tier 1 — dead weight (43 skills, ~6,663 tokens)\n67\t\n68\tHighest confidence. No judgment calls.\n69\t\n70\t- **Broken tools (9):** `Interceptor` `Browser` `playwright-cli` `firecrawl`\n71\t  `firecrawl-build-onboarding` `BrightData` `Apify` `web-scraping` `everything-search`\n72\t  — binaries not installed.\n73\t- **Generic thinking / prompt skills (21):** `caveman` `zoom-out` `roast` `BeCreative`\n74\t  `Ideate` `FirstPrinciples` `SystemsThinking` `Aphorisms` `Prompting` `BiasCheck`\n75\t  `IterativeDepth` `ApertureOscillation` `BitterPillEngineering` `ExtractWisdom`\n76\t  `Council` `grill-me` `grill-with-docs` `backtrack` `fact-checker` `Fabric`\n77\t  — this is *exactly* the category the video says to delete. Opus 5 does these natively.\n78\t- **Not your domain (13):** `pp-flight-goat` `pp-movie-goat` `pp-recipe-goat` `Sales`\n79\t  `starter-icp-positioning` `starter-voice-profile` `USMetrics` `WorldThreatModel`\n80\t  `RedTeam` `PrivateInvestigator` `Art` `AudioEditor` `Remotion` `WriteStory`\n81\t\n82\t### Tier 2 — superseded (56 skills, ~6,137 tokens)\n83\t\n84\tYou already use something that covers each of these. Contains judgment calls —\n85\treview before running.\n86\t\n87\t- **Skill authoring** — `CreateSkill` (22 uses) covers: `write-a-skill`\n88\t  `writing-great-skills` `skill-evaluator` `find-skills`\n89\t- **Matt Pocock duplicates** — you invoke the `mattpocock-skills:*` plugin versions;\n90\t  these are stale local copies: `ask-matt` `setup-matt-pocock-skills` `codebase-design`\n91\t  `diagnosing-bugs` `domain-modeling` `tdd` `research`\n92\t- **Design pile** — `impeccable` (6) + `artifact-design` (8) cover: `gpt-taste`\n93\t  `high-end-visual-design` `image-to-code` `imagegen-frontend-*` `industrial-brutalist-ui`\n94\t  `minimalist-ui` `redesign-existing-projects` `stitch-design-taste` `design-academy-skill`\n95\t  `starter-design-tokens` `brandkit` `Webdesign`\n96\t  `frontend-slides` `visual-explainer` `diagram-generator`\n97\t- **Workflow pile** — `superpowers:*` + `claudex-*` cover: `to-prd` `to-spec` `to-tickets`\n98\t  `triage` `implement` `wayfinder` `improve-codebase-architecture` `RootCauseAnalysis`\n99\t  `loop-designer` `Loop` `Delegation` `Migrate` `Optimize` `Hardening` `decision-toolkit`\n100\t  `CreateCLI` `Agents` `Evals` `ContextSearch` `Daemon` `LocalIntelligence` `Knowledge`\n101\t  `Interview` `process-interviewer` `research-assistant` `storm-research`\n102\t  `full-output-enforcement` `fable-mode` `Telos`\n103\t\n104\t### Keep — tacit knowledge, even at zero uses\n105\t\n106\tThese carry knowledge the model can never have. The video is explicit that this is\n107\tthe one category worth keeping forever.\n108\t\n109\t`game-film-timestamps` (Hudl/DVSport/ESPN timestamp repair) ·\n110\t`pp-catapult-openfield-connect` (GPS) · `pp-zotero-research-library` ·\n111\t`five-slides-generator` (your Baylor deck format) · `pp-fireflies`\n112\t\n113\t### Grace period — installed in the last 14 days\n114\t\n115\t`new-project` `brain-audit` `codex-build` `claudex-route` `claudex-loop`\n116\t`next-decision` `decisions` `before-building` `anti-sleep` `persistent-localhost`\n117\t`session-miner` `improve-system` `design-taste-frontend-v1`\n118\t\n119\t### Your call — not cut, not defended\n120\t\n121\t`pbir-report-builder` (Power BI / IBCS — plausibly useful for Baylor reporting,\n122\tunused 47 days) · `Science` · `ArXiv` · `pp-espn` · `weekly-review` ·\n123\t`ingest-resource` · `library-advisor` · `library-review` · `capture-insight` ·\n124\t`scroll-craft`\n125\t\n126\t## Result\n127\t\n128\t| Stage | Skills | Roster cost | Per-session tokens |\n129\t|---|---|---|---|\n130\t| Now | 160 | 76,632 ch | ~19,158 |\n131\t| After Tier 1 | 117 | 49,980 ch | ~12,495 |\n132\t| After Tier 2 | **61** | 25,430 ch | **~6,357** |\n133\t\n134\t**~12,800 tokens back every session — a 66% cut.**\n135\t\n136\t## How to run it\n137\t\n138\tThe script **archives, never deletes.** Everything moves to\n139\t`~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/`.\n140\t\n141\t```bash\n142\tbash ~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh dryrun   # show, move nothing\n143\tbash ~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh tier1\n144\tbash ~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh tier2\n145\t```\n146\t\n147\tUndo, any time:\n148\t\n149\t```bash\n150\tmv ~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/<name> ~/.claude/skills/   # one skill\n151\tmv ~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/* ~/.claude/skills/        # all of them\n152\t```\n153\t\n154\tThen `/reload-skills` or start a new session.\n155\t\n156\t## Next steps after this\n157\t\n158\t1. **Promotion rule.** You have 0 project-level skills. New skills start in\n159\t   `<project>/.claude/skills/` and only move to global once they prove out across\n160\t   2+ projects. See `project_skill-bloat-and-promotion`.\n161\t2. **Plugin side.** ~37 plugin skills load per session from 6 enabled plugins. That is\n162\t   a separate, smaller pass — done by disabling whole plugins, not individual skills.\n163\t   (The 606 SKILL.md files in `~/.claude/plugins/cache/` are mostly disabled plugins and\n164\t   cached old versions. They are disk clutter, not context cost.)\n165\t3. **Put it on a clock.** Monthly skill audit, weekly rules review. The decay table\n166\t   is in the companion note."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"71716f28-032b-4f62-a526-72ed0a3f98b0","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:06:10.682Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-skill-audit.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t---\n2\ttitle: \"Skill audit 2026-09-12 — 160 global skills down to 60\"\n3\tdate: 2026-09-12\n4\ttype: audit\n5\ttrigger: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6LNlCpQPYFc\n6\trelated: 2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md\n7\tscript: ~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh\n8\ttags: [skills, context-engineering, claude-code, audit]\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t# Skill audit — 2026-09-12\n12\t\n13\t> ## STATUS\n14\t> - **Tier 1: EXECUTED 2026-09-12.** 43 skills archived to\n15\t>   `~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/`. Global skills 160 → **117**.\n16\t>   Regression check clean — **none** of the 43 had ever been invoked.\n17\t>   Roster cost 19,158 → **12,495 tokens** per session.\n18\t> - **Tier 2: NOT RUN.** 56 skills, ~6,137 tokens. Awaiting review.\n19\t> - Hook safety checked: `ArtWorkflowGuard` and `containment-zones` reference\n20\t>   archived paths but both degrade safely (try/catch → `[]`, and static strings).\n21\t>   Nothin