{"parentUuid":"ee3aca37-7047-4c5d-b006-3c04cba9067b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceyg4SvxkE6YozyhQ9bpM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done and verified. Here is what happened.\n\n## What I changed on your machine\n\nI moved **43 unused skills** out of `~/.claude/skills/`. They are not deleted — they sit in `~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/`.\n\n**Undo anything, any time:**\n```\nmv ~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/* ~/.claude/skills/\n```\n\nRun `/reload-skills` (or start a new session) to see the change.\n\n## Did it work\n\nYes. I checked three things:\n\n- **Nothing you use got cut.** All 43 had *never* been invoked in 414 sessions. Zero regressions.\n- **No hooks broke.** Two hooks pointed at archived folders. Both handle a missing folder safely. I checked the code.\n- **Skills went 160 → 117.** Your skill list costs **~12,495 tokens** per session now, down from **~19,158**.\n\n## Two things I got wrong earlier, now fixed\n\n1. **\"606 plugin skills\" was wrong.** That was disk cache. Only **6 plugins are enabled** (18 are off), so about **37** plugin skills actually load. I corrected this in all 5 files.\n2. **45 of your skills are symlinks** into `~/.agents/skills/` — the folder Codex also reads. Archiving a symlink only unhooks it from Claude Code. Codex keeps its copy. Good news, but worth knowing.\n\nAlso worth knowing: `~/.claude/skills/` is **gitignored**. Git will not save you here. The archive folder is the only undo.\n\n## Saved to memory\n\n- `project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md` — the numbers, the promotion rule, the re-measure command, the 3 traps above.\n- Your Active Threads now says: Tier 1 done, Tier 2 pending.\n\n## Files\n\n| What | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Video breakdown | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md` |\n| Audit report | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-skill-audit.md` |\n| The script | `~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh` |\n\n## Your one decision\n\nTier 2 is loaded and ready: **56 more skills**, worth another **~6,100 tokens** a session. That would take you to 61 skills.\n\n| Option | Why |\n|---|---|\n| **Run Tier 2** ⭐ | Doubles the saving. Every one is covered by a skill you already use (`CreateSkill`, `impeccable`, `superpowers:*`, the `mattpocock-skills:*` plugin). Same one-command undo. |\n| Stop at Tier 1 | Tier 2 has judgment calls. If you want to eyeball the list first, it is in the audit report under \"Tier 2\". |\n\n**I would run it.** The genuinely uncertain ones I already pulled out into a \"your call\" list and left alone.\n\nSay the word and I will run `tier2`.\n\nresult: Tier 1 skill audit executed and verified — 43 never-used skills archived reversibly, Claude Code roster 160→117 skills and ~19.2k→12.5k tokens per session, zero regressions and no broken hooks; video breakdown + audit report written to `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/`, findings saved to memory, and Tier 2 (56 skills, ~6.1k more tokens) is staged awaiting your go."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_read_input_tokens":201119,"output_tokens":1285,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":132},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":201119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1124},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ceyg4S7M3dnJozS1k4WVk","attributionSkill":"memory-write","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2971f6d-9477-48d9-9130-141180fde8e1","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:06