{"parentUuid":"c98450ca-188b-47f2-922b-9bac7a605f0d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0c142cad-0b6f-4d85-a335-7763a49aa9c2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015AcQW1gkaXvEz6CLPgoZDd","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pi Documentation Structure\n\n## Main Sections & Pages\n\n**Getting Started**\n- Quickstart\n- Using Pi\n- Providers\n\n**Core Features**\n- llama.cpp (local model routing)\n- Security\n- Containerization\n- Settings\n- Keybindings\n- Sessions\n- Compaction\n\n**Customization**\n- Extensions\n- Skills\n- Prompt templates\n- Themes\n- Pi packages\n- Custom models\n- Custom providers\n\n**Integration**\n- SDK\n- RPC mode\n- JSON event stream mode\n- TUI components\n\n**Reference**\n- Environment variables\n- Session format\n\n**Platform Setup**\n- Windows, Termux, tmux, Terminal setup, Shell aliases\n\n**Development**\n\n---\n\n## Core Architecture & Concepts\n\n**Foundation:** Pi is described as \"a minimal terminal coding harness\" that maintains a lean core while remaining extensible.\n\n**Extensions:** TypeScript modules that add tools, commands, event handlers, and custom UI capabilities to Pi.\n\n**Skills:** Agent capabilities that can be reused on-demand, invoked through slash commands or programmatically.\n\n**Configuration:** Operates through multiple layers—global settings, project-specific settings, environment variables, and custom keybindings. Authentication supports both API keys (like `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) and subscription provider login via `/login`.\n\n**Extensibility Model:** Users can bundle and distribute customizations as Pi packages, combining extensions, skills, prompts, and themes together."}]},"uuid":"726deada-7707-4e63-a2f5-0571d6c2db42","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:21:59.586Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":3365,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Pi Documentation Structure\n\n## Main Sections & Pages\n\n**Getting Started**\n- Quickstart\n- Using Pi\n- Providers\n\n**Core Features**\n- llama.cpp (local model routing)\n- Security\n- Containerization\n- Settings\n- Keybindings\n- Sessions\n- Compaction\n\n**Customization**\n- Extensions\n- Skills\n- Prompt templates\n- Themes\n- Pi packages\n- Custom models\n- Custom providers\n\n**Integration**\n- SDK\n- RPC mode\n- JSON event stream mode\n- TUI components\n\n**Reference**\n- Environment variables\n- Session format\n\n**Platform Setup**\n- Windows, Termux, tmux, Terminal setup, Shell aliases\n\n**Development**\n\n---\n\n## Core Architecture & Concepts\n\n**Foundation:** Pi is described as \"a minimal terminal coding harness\" that maintains a lean core while remaining extensible.\n\n**Extensions:** TypeScript modules that add tools, commands, event handlers, and custom UI capabilities to Pi.\n\n**Skills:** Agent capabilities that can be reused on-demand, invoked through slash commands or programmatically.\n\n**Configuration:** Operates through multiple layers—global settings, project-specific settings, environment variables, and custom keybindings. Authentication supports both API keys (like `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) and subscription provider login via `/login`.\n\n**Extensibility Model:** Users can bundle and distribute customizations as Pi packages, combining extensions, skills, prompts, and themes together.","durationMs":4549,"url":"https://pi.dev/docs/latest"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c98450ca-188b-47f2-922b-9bac7a605f0d","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
