{"parentUuid":"8269158f-030f-417c-a5d5-7bb1287124ea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0c142cad-0b6f-4d85-a335-7763a49aa9c2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rp2jrvDxRkLdB9mZ49LCAu","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pi Model Providers & Authentication\n\n## Supported Providers\n\nPi supports numerous model providers including:\n\n**Subscription-based:** ChatGPT Plus/Pro, Claude Pro/Max, GitHub Copilot, xAI (Grok), OpenRouter, Radius\n\n**API Key providers:** Anthropic, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Google Gemini, Azure OpenAI, Amazon Bedrock, Mistral, Groq, Cloudflare, xAI, and 20+ others\n\n## Claude Pro/Max Support\n\nYes, Pi supports Claude Pro/Max accounts. As documented, \"Third-party harness usage draws from extra usage and is billed per token, not against Claude plan limits.\"\n\n## Switching Models Mid-Session\n\nUse the `/model` command to switch models during an interactive session. For llama.cpp, use `/llama` to manage loaded models.\n\n## Authentication Methods\n\n**Priority order for credential resolution:**\n1. CLI `--api-key` flag\n2. Entries in `~/.pi/agent/auth.json`\n3. Environment variables\n4. Custom provider keys from `models.json`\n\n**API key environment variables** (examples):\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` → Anthropic\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` → OpenAI\n- `GEMINI_API_KEY` → Google Gemini\n- `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` → Amazon Bedrock\n\n**Subscription login:** Use `/login` in interactive mode to authenticate with OAuth providers."}]},"uuid":"a3e5a95c-f29b-40e3-94fb-5b2eeb55eb0f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:22:41.736Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":14389,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Pi Model Providers & Authentication\n\n## Supported Providers\n\nPi supports numerous model providers including:\n\n**Subscription-based:** ChatGPT Plus/Pro, Claude Pro/Max, GitHub Copilot, xAI (Grok), OpenRouter, Radius\n\n**API Key providers:** Anthropic, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Google Gemini, Azure OpenAI, Amazon Bedrock, Mistral, Groq, Cloudflare, xAI, and 20+ others\n\n## Claude Pro/Max Support\n\nYes, Pi supports Claude Pro/Max accounts. As documented, \"Third-party harness usage draws from extra usage and is billed per token, not against Claude plan limits.\"\n\n## Switching Models Mid-Session\n\nUse the `/model` command to switch models during an interactive session. For llama.cpp, use `/llama` to manage loaded models.\n\n## Authentication Methods\n\n**Priority order for credential resolution:**\n1. CLI `--api-key` flag\n2. Entries in `~/.pi/agent/auth.json`\n3. Environment variables\n4. Custom provider keys from `models.json`\n\n**API key environment variables** (examples):\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` → Anthropic\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` → OpenAI\n- `GEMINI_API_KEY` → Google Gemini\n- `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` → Amazon Bedrock\n\n**Subscription login:** Use `/login` in interactive mode to authenticate with OAuth providers.","durationMs":4769,"url":"https://pi.dev/docs/latest/providers"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8269158f-030f-417c-a5d5-7bb1287124ea","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"406a854b-9ffa-4690-a821-a0820beeb2d4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0c142cad-0b6f-4d85-a335-7763a49aa9c2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qKNcdZnQ2SN6LebBd3diF","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pi Settings: Architecture and Configuration\n\n## Settings Layers & File Locations\n\nPi uses a two-tier settings hierarchy:\n\n| Layer | Path | Scope |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| Global | `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` | All projects |\n| Project | `.pi/settings.json` | Current directory only |\n\nProject-level configurations take precedence, with nested objects merging recursively rather than replacing entirely.\n\n## Key Configuration Categories\n\n### Model & Thinking\n- `defaultProvider`, `defaultModel`: Startup model selection\n- `defaultThinkingLevel`: Initial thinking mode (`\"off\"` through `\"max\"`)\n- `modelThinkingLevels`: Per-model thinking overrides\n- `hideThinkingBlock`, `showCacheMissNotices`: Display preferences\n\n### Resources & Extensions\nThe `skills` setting enables loading custom skill implementations:\n\n> \"Local skill file paths or directories\"\n\nAdditional resource keys include:\n- `packages`: npm/git packages containing resources\n- `extensions`: Local extension file paths\n- `prompts`: Prompt template directories\n- `themes`: Custom theme locations\n- `enableSkillCommands`: Register skills as `/skill:name` commands\n\n### UI & Display\n- `theme`, `externalEditor`: Visual preferences\n- `quietStartup`, `tuiMode`: Startup behavior\n- `outputPad`, `editorPaddingX`: Spacing controls\n- `fullscreenScrollbar`, `fullscreenCopyOnSelect`: Advanced TUI options\n\n### Compaction & Performance\n- `compaction.enabled`, `compaction.reserveTokens`: Auto-compaction settings\n- `compaction.modelOverrides`: Per-model token budgets\n- `branchSummary.reserveTokens`: Branch history summarization\n\n### Transport & Network\n- `transport`: Preferred delivery mechanism (`\"sse\"`, `\"websocket\"`, `\"auto\"`)\n- `httpProxy`: Global proxy configuration\n- `retry`: Exponential backoff and timeout settings\n\n### Terminal & Images\n- `terminal.showImages`, `terminal.imageWidthCells`: Image rendering\n- `images.autoResize`, `images.blockImages`: Image handling\n\n## Settings Merging Behavior\n\nProject and global settings combine recursively before model selection occurs. This approach allows granular overrides:\n\n```json\n// Global: broad defaults\n{ \"compaction\": { \"enabled\": true, \"reserveTokens\": 16384 } }\n\n// Project: narrow override\n{ \"compaction\": { \"reserveTokens\": 8192 } }\n\n// Result: merged\n{ \"compaction\": { \"enabled\": true, \"reserveTokens\": 8192 } }\n```\n\nA project setting for a specific model takes priority over global model-specific values without replacing other models or fields."}]},"uuid":"8c63f393-651f-411a-99e6-2812197f32c1","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:22:42.945Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":19232,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Pi Settings: Architecture and Configuration\n\n## Settings Layers & File Locations\n\nPi uses a two-tier settings hierarchy:\n\n| Layer | Path | Scope |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| Global | `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` | All projects |\n| Project | `.pi/settings.json` | Current directory only |\n\nProject-level configurations take precedence, with nested objects merging recursively rather than replacing entirely.\n\n## Key Configuration Categories\n\n### Model & Thinking\n- `defaultProvider`, `defaultModel`: Startup model selection\n- `defaultThinkingLevel`: Initial thinking mode (`\"off\"` through `\"max\"`)\n- `modelThinkingLevels`: Per-model thinking overrides\n- `hideThinkingBlock`, `showCacheMissNotices`: Display preferences\n\n### Resources & Extensions\nThe `skills` setting enables loading custom skill implementations:\n\n> \"Local skill file paths or directories\"\n\nAdditional resource keys include:\n- `packages`: npm/git packages containing resources\n- `extensions`: Local extension file paths\n- `prompts`: Prompt template directories\n- `themes`: Custom theme locations\n- `enableSkillCommands`: Register skills as `/skill:name` commands\n\n### UI & Display\n- `theme`, `externalEditor`: Visual preferences\n- `quietStartup`, `tuiMode`: Startup behavior\n- `outputPad`, `editorPaddingX`: Spacing controls\n- `fullscreenScrollbar`, `fullscreenCopyOnSelect`: Advanced TUI options\n\n### Compaction & Performance\n- `compaction.enabled`, `compaction.reserveTokens`: Auto-compaction settings\n- `compaction.modelOverrides`: Per-model token budgets\n- `branchSummary.reserveTokens`: Branch history summarization\n\n### Transport & Network\n- `transport`: Preferred delivery mechanism (`\"sse\"`, `\"websocket\"`, `\"auto\"`)\n- `httpProxy`: Global proxy configuration\n- `retry`: Exponential backoff and timeout settings\n\n### Terminal & Images\n- `terminal.showImages`, `terminal.imageWidthCells`: Image rendering\n- `images.autoResize`, `images.blockImages`: Image handling\n\n## Settings Merging Behavior\n\nProject and global settings combine recursively before model selection occurs. This approach allows granular overrides:\n\n```json\n// Global: broad defaults\n{ \"compaction\": { \"enabled\": true, \"reserveTokens\": 16384 } }\n\n// Project: narrow override\n{ \"compaction\": { \"reserveTokens\": 8192 } }\n\n// Result: merged\n{ \"compaction\": { \"enabled\": true, \"reserveTokens\": 8192 } }\n```\n\nA project setting for a specific model takes priority over global model-specific values without replacing other models or fields.","durationMs":8995,"url":"https://pi.dev/docs/latest/settings"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"406a854b-9ffa-4690-a821-a0820beeb2d4","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"3c5f138b-fb28-4862-a332-ca5ae734d96e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0c142cad-0b6f-4d85-a335-7763a49aa9c2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UK8LKPLbT3T2qVo25aRAkC","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pi's Context Compaction and Session Management\n\n## Automatic and Manual Compaction\n\nPi handles context through two compaction approaches:\n\n**Automatic compaction** triggers when \"contextTokens > contextWindow - reserveTokens\" (16,384 tokens by default). This occurs during multi-turn agent runs after tools complete, before new user prompts, or when context exceeds thresholds.\n\n**Manual compaction** uses the `/compact [instructions]` command to summarize older content on demand, with optional focus parameters.\n\n## How Compaction Works\n\nThe process identifies a \"cut point\" by working backward through messages until reaching `keepRecentTokens` (default 20,000). Messages before this point get summarized while recent work is preserved. The system:\n\n1. Extracts older messages for summarization\n2. Calls the LLM with structured format\n3. Stores a `CompactionEntry` containing the summary and file tracking data\n4. Rebuilds context using the summary plus retained messages\n\nNotably, \"tool results are truncated to 2000 characters during serialization\" to manage token costs.\n\n## Branch Navigation and Session Tree\n\nThe `/tree` command navigates a branching session history. When switching branches, Pi offers to create a `BranchSummaryEntry` summarizing work from the abandoned branch. This injects relevant context into the new branch while maintaining separate conversation paths.\n\n## Key Settings\n\nConfigure behavior via `~/.pi/agent/settings.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compaction\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"reserveTokens\": 16384,\n    \"keepRecentTokens\": 20000\n  }\n}\n```\n\nModel-specific overrides adjust token budgets per LLM, useful for models with larger context windows."}]},"uuid":"db5ae47f-a899-4912-bb19-af7cf9779158","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:22:44.110Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":21186,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Pi's Context Compaction and Session Management\n\n## Automatic and Manual Compaction\n\nPi handles context through two compaction approaches:\n\n**Automatic compaction** triggers when \"contextTokens > contextWindow - reserveTokens\" (16,384 tokens by default). This occurs during multi-turn agent runs after tools complete, before new user prompts, or when context exceeds thresholds.\n\n**Manual compaction** uses the `/compact [instructions]` command to summarize older content on demand, with optional focus parameters.\n\n## How Compaction Works\n\nThe process identifies a \"cut point\" by working backward through messages until reaching `keepRecentTokens` (default 20,000). Messages before this point get summarized while recent work is preserved. The system:\n\n1. Extracts older messages for summarization\n2. Calls the LLM with structured format\n3. Stores a `CompactionEntry` containing the summary and file tracking data\n4. Rebuilds context using the summary plus retained messages\n\nNotably, \"tool results are truncated to 2000 characters during serialization\" to manage token costs.\n\n## Branch Navigation and Session Tree\n\nThe `/tree` command navigates a branching session history. When switching branches, Pi offers to create a `BranchSummaryEntry` summarizing work from the abandoned branch. This injects relevant context into the new branch while maintaining separate conversation paths.\n\n## Key Settings\n\nConfigure behavior via `~/.pi/agent/settings.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compaction\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"reserveTokens\": 16384,\n    \"keepRecentTokens\": 20000\n  }\n}\n```\n\nModel-specific overrides adjust token budgets per LLM, useful for models with larger context windows.","durationMs":6074,"url":"https://pi.dev/docs/latest/compaction"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c5f138b-fb28-4862-a332-ca5ae734d96e","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
