{"parentUuid":"f6b59595-1274-4261-8683-f2b4bc6216f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeyhPVTR19CNHFov93B9z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RCymnVBkgfPfRgaC9nA8io","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md\"\nt=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold=\"\"\"2. **Your skills port. Your hooks do not.** Skill markdown and `CLAUDE.md` content move\n   over with editing. But your 61 hooks, `keystone-unified-snapshot.js`, the statusline,\n   and the session-start injection are all Claude-Code-shaped. In Pi they would be\n   rewritten as extensions. The video's \"one harness for everything\" glosses over this —\n   it is weeks of work, not an afternoon.\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"2. **Your skills port with one line of config — your hooks need a real but bounded port.**\n   ~~Skills port with editing; hooks would be a rewrite of weeks.~~ **Corrected after\n   reading the docs** (see `2026-09-12-pi-harness-research.md`): Pi implements the same\n   Agent Skills standard, already auto-discovers `~/.agents/skills/` where 45 of your\n   skills live, and loads `CLAUDE.md` directly. Hooks become TypeScript *extensions* —\n   your hooks are already TypeScript, and Pi's `tool_call` event returns\n   `{block, reason}`, which is exactly your `dcg` guard. One deliberate port per hook,\n   not a paradigm rewrite.\n3. **Running your Claude subscription through Pi costs extra.** Per Pi's docs,\n   third-party harness usage \"draws from extra usage and is billed per token, not\n   against Claude plan limits.\" The video's \"swap the brain freely\" pitch quietly\n   assumes you are paying per token anyway.\"\"\"\nassert old in t\nt=t.replace(old,new,1)\nold2=\"\"\"3. **\"24 hours to swap everything\"** (16:15) is Kashef's claim about *his* assets,\n   which he deliberately built provider-agnostic from day one. Yours are not yet.\"\"\"\nnew2=\"\"\"4. **\"24 hours to swap everything\"** (16:15) is Kashef's claim about *his* assets,\n   which he deliberately built provider-agnostic from day one. Yours are closer than\n   I first thought — but the safety layer is the part that does not come free.\"\"\"\nassert old2 in t\nt=t.replace(old2,new2,1)\nold3=\"\"\"Pi is real and worth trying. But it is a **harness you have to build**, not a harness\nyou get. Your leverage right now is not a new harness — it is that you load ~200 skills\nper session and use about 30. Fix that first. The audit makes any future harness move\ncheaper, because you would be porting 30 good skills instead of 200 mixed ones.\"\"\"\nnew3=\"\"\"Pi is real and worth trying. But it is a **harness you have to build**, not a harness\nyou get. The skills and context files move almost for free; the permission prompts,\nguards and approval flows are all yours to re-create.\n\n**Status 2026-09-12:** the skill audit is DONE — 99 skills archived, 160 → 61 global,\n~19.2k → ~6.4k tokens per session. Full Pi research is in\n`2026-09-12-pi-harness-research.md`. Next step there is a 30-minute sandbox trial in\n`~/pi-trial`, then porting one hook (`dcg`) to measure the true cost of a full move.\"\"\"\nassert old3 in t\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(t.replace(old3,new3,1))\nprint(\"video note corrected\")\nPY\ngrep -n \"weeks of work\" /Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md || echo \"stale claim removed ✓\"","description":"Correct the Pi claims in the video note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5213,"cache_read_input_tokens":225301,"output_tokens":1345,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5213,"ephemeral_5m_i