{"parentUuid":"87241232-cef8-4dc9-9ff5-2ed6f450cb85","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeyhTsg1BxLbzubzCURe7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1451,"cache_read_input_tokens":234198,"output_tokens":1816,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":183},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1451,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1816,"cache_read_input_tokens":234198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1451},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeyhTrhTCeG5h2KsKLgeh","type":"assistant","uuid":"176cefbe-e6cb-46f3-ab5f-c053dd2ec253","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:24:54.682Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"176cefbe-e6cb-46f3-ab5f-c053dd2ec253","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeyhTsg1BxLbzubzCURe7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All verified. Here is the whole picture.\n\n## 1. Tier 2 ran\n\n**99 skills archived total. You went from 160 → 61.**\n\n| | Before | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| Global skills | 160 | **61** |\n| Tokens per session | ~19,158 | **~6,428** |\n\nThat is a **66% cut**. About 12,700 tokens handed back every session.\n\nChecks passed:\n- **Zero of all 99** archived skills had ever been used. No regressions.\n- **5 hooks smoke-tested.** All exit clean. Nothing broke.\n- All your Baylor skills still live (`game-film-timestamps`, `pp-catapult-openfield-connect`, `five-slides-generator`, etc).\n\nUndo any time: `mv ~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/* ~/.claude/skills/`\n\n## 2. Matt Pocock + superpowers — both safe\n\nGood news: there was never a real conflict.\n\nBoth **plugins are untouched and still enabled** — `mattpocock-skills` (35 skills) and `superpowers` (14 skills).\n\nWhat I archived were **old local copies** of the same skills, symlinked from July. The plugin ships **all** of them and is newer (v1.2.3). So you did not lose `ask-matt`, `tdd`, `research`, `codebase-design`, `triage`, `implement` — you now get the fresher plugin version instead of two copies fighting.\n\nNew rule saved to memory: **when a plugin and a local skill share a name, the plugin wins.**\n\n## 3. Pi research — I was wrong about two things\n\nI read the full docs. Two corrections to what I told you this morning:\n\n**Wrong #1 — I said your skills would need editing. They do not.**\nPi uses the **same skill standard** as Claude Code. It already looks in `~/.agents/skills/` by default — that is where 45 of your skills live. For the rest, one line:\n```json\n{ \"skills\": [\"~/.claude/skills\"] }\n```\nIt also reads `CLAUDE.md` directly. Your context files move as-is.\n\n**Wrong #2 — I said hooks were \"weeks of work.\" Too pessimistic.**\nPi hooks are called **extensions**, written in TypeScript. Your hooks are *already* TypeScript. And Pi's docs show this example:\n```typescript\npi.on(\"tool_call\", async (event, ctx) => {\n  if (event.input.command?.includes(\"rm -rf\")) return { block: true, reason: \"Blocked\" };\n});\n```\nThat is your `dcg` guard, almost exactly. It is a real port, but it is refactoring — not starting over.\n\n**New thing I found that the video never says:**\nRunning your Claude subscription through Pi **bills per token as \"extra usage\"**. It does *not* count against your plan. That changes the money story of \"just swap the brain.\"\n\n**The safety warning still stands, and it is worse than I thought.** Straight from the docs: *\"Pi does not include a built-in sandbox.\"* No approval prompts at all. Never point it at `~/DEV` or anything near `DexaProject`.\n\n## Files\n\n| What | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Pi research (new) | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-pi-harness-research.md` |\n| Video breakdown | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md` |\n| Audit record | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-skill-audit.md` |\n| The script | `~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh` |\n\nMemory updated with the audit result, the plugin-wins rule, and the verified Pi facts.\n\n## What to do now\n\nRun `/reload-skills` (or restart) to pick up the leaner skill list.\n\nWhen you want Pi, it is a 30-minute safe trial:\n```\nmkdir -p ~/pi-trial && cd ~/pi-trial\nnpm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\npi\n```\nThen `/login` inside it. Throwaway folder, nothing of yours at risk. Say the word and I will walk it with you.\n\nresult: Tier 2 executed — 99 skills archived total, Claude Code went 160→61 global skills and ~19.2k→6.4k tokens per session (66% cut) with zero regressions and all 5 hooks smoke-tested clean; mattpocock-skills and superpowers plugins verified intact (only stale local duplicates removed); full Pi documentation research written to `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-pi-harness-research.md`, correcting two earlier claims — Pi reads your existing skills and CLAUDE.md with one config line, hooks port as TypeScript extensions rather than a rewrite, but Pi ships no sandbox and bills Claude subscriptions per-token as extra usage."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1451,"cache_read_input_tokens":234198,"output_tokens":1816,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":183},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1451,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1816,"cache_read_input_tokens":234198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1451},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CeyhTrhTCeG5h2KsKLgeh","type":"assistant","uuid":"a397eac8-05c0-476d-9038-dc2551df1dd8","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:25:15.495Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
