{"parentUuid":"120bce2a-6405-41b3-b3bd-a770865813b0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"11a6ada2-1325-409e-a2ef-4046c9c2c771","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LknNc4GccnkRb5b6DootPC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Anthropic Claude Pro Max subscription third-party harness \"extra usage\" billed per token not plan limits\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Anthropic to limit Using third-party harnesses with Claude subscriptions | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47633568\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic reinstates OpenClaw and third-party agent usage on Claude subscriptions — with a catch | VentureBeat\",\"url\":\"https://venturebeat.com/technology/anthropic-reinstates-openclaw-and-third-party-agent-usage-on-claude-subscriptions-with-a-catch\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic Just Killed Third-Party Harnesses and I'm Properly Gutted - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/stevengonsalvez/anthropic-just-killed-third-party-harnesses-and-im-properly-gutted-dfk\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Max, third-party harnesses and the extra credit offer: why developers are angry\",\"url\":\"https://blog.mikecodeur.com/en/post/claude-max-third-party-harness-extra-credit-offer\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic Just Pulled the Rug on Third-Party Claude Tools.\",\"url\":\"https://permaship.ai/blog/anthropic-just-pulled-the-rug-on-third-party-claude-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic Extra Usage: Harnesses, Credits, PBC Charges\",\"url\":\"https://ccleaks.com/news/anthropic-kills-third-party-harnesses\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic Subscription Auth Warning: Third-Party Usage Draws From Extra Usage, Not Your Plan - Fazm Blog\",\"url\":\"https://fazm.ai/blog/anthropic-subscription-auth-warning-third-party-extra-usage\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic Banned Third-Party Claude Auth: Full Guide 2026 | KERSAI\",\"url\":\"https://kersai.com/anthropic-killed-third-party-claude-access-heres-every-workaround-that-still-works/\"},{\"title\":\"19383954 ymmv anthropic claude 100 extra usage claim in account\",\"url\":\"https://slickdeals.net/f/19383954-ymmv-anthropic-claude-100-extra-usage-claim-in-account\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Anthropic's Claude Pro and Max subscription policy regarding third-party harnesses and extra usage billing:\n\n## Policy Change (April 4, 2026)\n\nEffective April 4, 2026 at 12:00 PM PT, Anthropic stopped allowing Claude Pro, Max, and Claude Code subscribers to use their monthly subscription limits for third-party harnesses and agents, most notably the popular tool OpenClaw.\n\n## How Extra Usage Billing Works\n\nExtra usage is pay-as-you-go at API rates, billed separately from the subscription, and often appears as Anthropic / Anthropic PBC charges. Every token the tool generates counts against your extra usage balance, not the usage allowance included in your monthly plan.\n\nOnce you use the claude -p command for non-interactive tasks, run a GitHub Action, or connect a third-party tool like OpenClaw, the system switches to the dedicated Agent SDK credit. Once the Agent SDK credit limit ($20 for Pro plans, $100 for Max 5X, etc) is exhausted, programmatic usage stops unless the user has enabled \"extra usage\" billing.\n\n## One-Time Credits Offered\n\n$20 / $100 / $200 \"on us\" credits were a one-time extra-usage promo for accounts subscribed by April 3, 2026 at 9 AM PT (Pro/Max/Team; Enterprise/Console excluded), claimable only through April 17, 2026 after enabling extra usage on web.\n\nThis represents a significant shift where third-party harness usage is now metered separately from standard subscription limits and charged per token rather than being covered under the flat monthly subscription fee.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"66a76606-31e2-41b9-a435-3cf3418f28fd","timestamp":"2026-09-12T14:49:42.478Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Anthropic Claude Pro Max subscription third-party harness \"extra usage\" billed per token not plan limits","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UYUXxy5UUYfXnwAjao8Ydg","content":[{"title":"Anthropic to limit Using third-party harnesses with Claude subscriptions | Hacker News","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47633568"},{"title":"Anthropic reinstates OpenClaw and third-party agent usage on Claude subscriptions — with a catch | VentureBeat","url":"https://venturebeat.com/technology/anthropic-reinstates-openclaw-and-third-party-agent-usage-on-claude-subscriptions-with-a-catch"},{"title":"Anthropic Just Killed Third-Party Harnesses and I'm Properly Gutted - DEV Community","url":"https://dev.to/stevengonsalvez/anthropic-just-killed-third-party-harnesses-and-im-properly-gutted-dfk"},{"title":"Claude Max, third-party harnesses and the extra credit offer: why developers are angry","url":"https://blog.mikecodeur.com/en/post/claude-max-third-party-harness-extra-credit-offer"},{"title":"Anthropic Just Pulled the Rug on Third-Party Claude Tools.","url":"https://permaship.ai/blog/anthropic-just-pulled-the-rug-on-third-party-claude-tools"},{"title":"Anthropic Extra Usage: Harnesses, Credits, PBC Charges","url":"https://ccleaks.com/news/anthropic-kills-third-party-harnesses"},{"title":"Anthropic Subscription Auth Warning: Third-Party Usage Draws From Extra Usage, Not Your Plan - Fazm Blog","url":"https://fazm.ai/blog/anthropic-subscription-auth-warning-third-party-extra-usage"},{"title":"Anthropic Banned Third-Party Claude Auth: Full Guide 2026 | KERSAI","url":"https://kersai.com/anthropic-killed-third-party-claude-access-heres-every-workaround-that-still-works/"},{"title":"19383954 ymmv anthropic claude 100 extra usage claim in account","url":"https://slickdeals.net/f/19383954-ymmv-anthropic-claude-100-extra-usage-claim-in-account"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Anthropic's Claude Pro and Max subscription policy regarding third-party harnesses and extra usage billing:\n\n## Policy Change (April 4, 2026)\n\nEffective April 4, 2026 at 12:00 PM PT, Anthropic stopped allowing Claude Pro, Max, and Claude Code subscribers to use their monthly subscription limits for third-party harnesses and agents, most notably the popular tool OpenClaw.\n\n## How Extra Usage Billing Works\n\nExtra usage is pay-as-you-go at API rates, billed separately from the subscription, and often appears as Anthropic / Anthropic PBC charges. Every token the tool generates counts against your extra usage balance, not the usage allowance included in your monthly plan.\n\nOnce you use the claude -p command for non-interactive tasks, run a GitHub Action, or connect a third-party tool like OpenClaw, the system switches to the dedicated Agent SDK credit. Once the Agent SDK credit limit ($20 for Pro plans, $100 for Max 5X, etc) is exhausted, programmatic usage stops unless the user has enabled \"extra usage\" billing.\n\n## One-Time Credits Offered\n\n$20 / $100 / $200 \"on us\" credits were a one-time extra-usage promo for accounts subscribed by April 3, 2026 at 9 AM PT (Pro/Max/Team; Enterprise/Console excluded), claimable only through April 17, 2026 after enabling extra usage on web.\n\nThis represents a significant shift where third-party harness usage is now metered separately from standard subscription limits and charged per token rather than being covered under the flat monthly subscription fee."],"durationSeconds":8.18421779099945,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"120bce2a-6405-41b3-b3bd-a770865813b0","session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
