{"parentUuid":"dea26880-59cc-42e1-ad1a-875d8cb8b1e5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"63776998-b36b-49c8-92b1-0e77176cf34f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T16:43:26.453Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"f1097c6d-9db5-4bb5-a0f7-c42d645cf75d","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"63776998-b36b-49c8-92b1-0e77176cf34f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceyt2q1M4CyfHP5Yu1nvF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BjNewbiqC2HAfjEQYsPJb5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-12-harness-skill-audit.md","content":"# Handoff — 2026-09-12 — harness video → skill audit → Pi research\n\nSession ran as a Claude Code background job. cwd `~/DEV`. Nothing was committed.\n\n## What this session did\n\n1. Watched a YouTube video on AI harnesses and wrote it up.\n2. Measured this machine's skill bloat, then **archived 99 of 160 global skills**.\n3. Researched the Pi harness (`pi.dev`) from its official docs.\n4. Answered a billing question about Claude subscriptions vs third-party harnesses.\n\n## Artifacts — read these, do not re-derive\n\n| Document | Path |\n|---|---|\n| Video breakdown + 11-point gap analysis | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-harness-over-model-mark-kashef.md` |\n| Skill audit record (has a STATUS block at top) | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-skill-audit.md` |\n| Pi research (docs breakdown + migration cost) | `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/2026-09-12-pi-harness-research.md` |\n| The archive script (tiered, reversible) | `~/.claude/skills-audit-2026-09-12.sh` |\n| Tier A memory (audit result + Pi facts + rules) | `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md` |\n\nSource video: `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6LNlCpQPYFc` — Nate Herk with Mark Kashef,\n\"How to Actually Choose the Right AI Agent\", 34 min, posted 2026-09-11.\n\n## Current state — verified, do not re-check casually\n\n- **Global skills: 160 → 61.** 99 archived to `~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/`.\n- **Roster cost: ~19,158 → ~6,428 tokens per session** (66% cut).\n- **Zero regressions.** None of the 99 had ever been invoked across 414 `.jsonl` sessions.\n- **Both tiers already ran.** The script is idempotent — a re-run reports \"not present\".\n  Do NOT run `tier1` or `tier2` again expecting work.\n- **Hooks verified.** `ArtWorkflowGuard`, `TelosSummarySync`, `TheRouter`,\n  `CommunicationSkillGuard`, `SuccessClaimGate` all smoke-tested and exit 0 with the\n  archived skills gone.\n- **Plugins untouched.** `mattpocock-skills` (35 skills, v1.2.3) and `superpowers`\n  (14 skills) both enabled and intact. User explicitly asked to keep both.\n- After the user ran `/reload-skills` + `/reload-plugins`: 104 skills, 6 plugins,\n  60 plugin skills, 7 agents, 20 hooks.\n\nUndo everything with one command:\n```bash\nmv ~/.claude/skills-archive/2026-09-12/* ~/.claude/skills/\n```\n\n## Decisions made this session\n\n1. **Skill audit before any Pi migration.** Leverage is the bloat, not the harness.\n2. **When a plugin and a local skill share a name, the plugin wins** — delete the local\n   copy. Applied to 7 Matt Pocock duplicates; the plugin ships all of them and is newer.\n3. **User will run Codex through his ChatGPT subscription inside Pi** — not Claude,\n   which avoids Anthropic's third-party per-token billing.\n\n## Traps discovered (all recorded in the Tier A memory file)\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is **gitignored** inside the `dotclaude` repo. Git is not a safety\n  net for skills; the archive folder is the only undo.\n- **45 of 160 skills were symlinks** into `~/.agents/skills/` (shared with Codex).\n  Count with `find -L`; plain `find` undercounts by 45. Archiving a symlink de-registers\n  it from Claude Code but leaves the real copy for Codex.\n- **\"606 plugin skills\" is cache, not load.** Only 6 of 24 plugins are enabled (~37\n  skills exposed). The rest are disabled plugins and old cached versions.\n- Counting skill usage from `.jsonl` requires filtering built-in CLI commands\n  (`/exit`, `/clear`, `/compact`…) or the total inflates from 58 to 74. The filtered\n  script is embedded in the Tier A memory file.\n- `dcg` blocks `find ... -delete`. Use an explicit `rm` on a named file instead.\n\n## Open / not done\n\n- **Tier 3 \"your call\" skills** were left alone, not cut, not defended:\n  `pbir-report-builder` `Science` `ArXiv` `pp-espn` `weekly-review` `ingest-resource`\n  `library-advisor` `library-review` `capture-insight` `scroll-craft`.\n- **Promotion rule not yet implemented.** There are still **0 project-level skills** in\n  `~/DEV`. New skills should start in `<project>/.claude/skills/` and only be promoted\n  to global after proving out across 2+ projects.\n- **No `rot.md`.** The decay-tier table (identity/substrate slow, skills+agents monthly,\n  rules weekly, hooks ~6 months) is written up in the video note but not yet a file.\n- **Monthly skill audit is not on a cron.** Currently a one-off.\n- **Pi is not installed.** Suggested 30-minute sandbox trial, never in `~/DEV`:\n  ```bash\n  mkdir -p ~/pi-trial && cd ~/pi-trial\n  npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\n  pi\n  ```\n  Then port one hook (`dcg`) to an extension to measure the true migration cost.\n- **Billing uncertainty, unresolved:** headless Claude use (`claude -p`, cron, GitHub\n  Actions, Agent SDK) was due to move to a separate credit pool on 2026-06-15, then\n  Anthropic paused that on 2026-06-16. Current status not confirmed from an Anthropic\n  page. Authoritative check is the user's own usage page.\n\n## Safety notes for the next agent\n\n- **Never point Pi at `~/DEV`**, and never near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete\n  health data, lives on Google Drive, not in `~/DEV`). Pi ships **no sandbox and no\n  approval prompts** — this is documented, deliberate design.\n- Two hooks exist in **two copies** (`~/.claude/hooks/` and `~/.codex/hooks/`). Patch both.\n- Global `MEMORY.md` is at 2,489 / 2,500 chars. Consolidate before adding anything.\n\n## Suggested skills\n\n| Skill | When to use it here |\n|---|---|\n| `memory-write` | Any new durable fact from the next session; also the retrieval ladder if you need past context. |\n| `CreateSkill` | If building the `/poly-skill` idea (dual-format Claude+Codex skills) or a `rot.md` audit skill. |\n| `update-config` | To put the monthly skill audit on a hook/cron, or to change `settings.json`. |\n| `claude-stack-doctor` | Verify the automation stack is still healthy after 99 skills moved. |\n| `doctor-plus` | Context-engineering audit — natural follow-on to the roster cut. |\n| `superpowers:brainstorming` | Before designing the promotion-rule rollout or the Pi extension port. |\n| `superpowers:verification-before-completion` | Before claiming any of the open items above are done. |\n| `closeout` | End of the next session — sweeps loose ends and writes the cross-harness handoff. |\n| `ingest-resource` | If the user wants the three Inbox notes promoted into proper vault entries. |\n| `Harvest` | If the skill audit is declared finished and worth distilling into `Knowledge/`. |\n\n## Suggested first move\n\nAsk the user which of these they want: (a) the promotion rule + `rot.md` + monthly cron,\n(b) the Pi sandbox trial, or (c) the Tier 3 \"your call\" skill decisions. All three are\nindependent. No sensitive data appears in this document.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":257668,"output_tokens":2934,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2934,"cache_read_input_tokens":257668,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"